      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Eastern Europe generally offers a highly skilled labor force with strong adherence to established manufacturing standards but typically requires intermediate management oversight to ensure consistent quality and productivity. Southeast Asia excels in labor-intensive environments with a growing technical skillset and eagerness to work, though consistency often depends on strict local supervision and rigorous training protocols. In contrast, Sub-Saharan Africa tends to feature lower average skill levels for complex industrial tasks, necessitating a significant hand-on leadership approach and on-the-job training to build effective teams.",
